      </profiles>
      <constraints>
        <constraint type="max" value="0" field="selections" scope="force" shared="true" id="9ca2-5450-6484-1651" includeChildSelections="true"/>
      </constraints>
      <modifiers>
        <modifier type="increment" value="3" field="9ca2-5450-6484-1651">
          <repeats>
            <repeat value="1000" repeats="1" field="limit::2085-9b6f-c588-0723" scope="force" childId="any" shared="true" roundUp="false" includeChildSelections="false" includeChildForces="false" percentValue="false"/>
          </repeats>
        </modifier>
      </modifiers>
      <rules>
        <rule name="Trolls" id="cfce-7a57-b66e-ac2a" hidden="false">
          <description>Trolls were known to stop and bite the throats of their victims in combat, so a unit of trolls may never advance more than 10 cm after combat.


Even though Trolls are quite stupid they have uncanny sense of smell. This sense of smell allows a unit of trolls to trace a LOS through friendly units to the enemy. A unit of Trolls will always use initiative to charge the closest enemy unit within 20cm, even if an unengaged friendly unit lies between the Trolls and their victims. When a unit of trolls is forced to charge an enemy unit and their path takes them through an unengaged friendly unit, a burst through is performed on the unit the Trolls were forced to move through. Remember this rule applies to unengaged friendly units only. Trolls will never trace a LOS through, charge through, or displace a friendly unit already in contact with the enemy.</description>
        </rule>
      </rules>
      <categoryLinks>
        <categoryLink name="Infantry" hidden="false" id="8225-a20a-2a7c-5445" targetId="5e38-77df-81d0-6399" primary="true"/>
      </categoryLinks>
    </selectionEntry>
